Sprint 1 Test Plan
1. Overview & Scope
The goal of Sprint 1 is to validate core authentication, user management, role-based access control (RBAC), and basic navigation.

Scope Items
Main Page
Login
Reset / Set Password
Register User
Main Landing Page (post-login)

User Roles
Superadmin: Full administrative control. Can block admins and users; can assign/set rights.
Admin: Moderate administrative control. Can block regular users; can assign/set user rights.
User: Standard user access without administrative or management rights.

Test Cases & Acceptance Criteria
Main Page
TC-01: Main Page Accessibility
Given an unauthenticated visitor accesses the application URL,
When the page loads,
Then the main public landing page displays correctly with options to Log In or Register.

Login
TC-02: Successful Login
Given a registered user enters valid credentials (email/username and password),
When they submit the login form,
Then they are authenticated and redirected to the main post-login landing page.

TC-03:Invalid Login
Given a user inputs invalid or incorrect credentials,
When they submit the login form,
Then an appropriate error message is displayed and access is denied.

TC-04:Blocked User Login Attempt
Given a user account has been blocked by an Admin or Superadmin,
When the user attempts to log in with valid credentials,
Then the system prevents access and displays an "Account Blocked" error message.

Reset / Set Password
TC-05: Request Password Reset Link
Given a user requests a password reset on the login page,
When they provide a registered email address,
Then a secure password reset link/token is sent to their email.

Set New Password
TC-06: Set New Password
Given a user clicks a valid password reset link,
When they enter a new password meeting system complexity guidelines and submit,
Then the password updates successfully, and they can log in using the new password.

Register User
TC-07: Successful User Registration
Given a new user fills out the registration form with valid required details,
When they submit the form,
Then the account is created, assignable default role permissions are set, and a confirmation email/message is generated.

TC-08: Registration Validation
Given a user submits the registration form with existing email addresses or missing mandatory fields,
When validation executes,
Then inline field errors prevent form submission.

Main Landing Page After Successful Login
TC-09: Post-Login Landing Page Navigation
Given an authenticated user successfully logs in,
When redirected to the post-login landing page,
Then the page loads correctly displaying user-specific options, user profile details, and navigation controls.

Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) & Rights Management
TC-10: Superadmin Permissions
Given a Superadmin user is logged in,
When managing accounts,
Then they can block/unblock both Admins and standard Users, as well as set/modify permissions for all roles.

TC-11: Admin Permissions & Constraints
Given an Admin user is logged in,
When managing accounts,
Then they can block/unblock standard Users and assign user rights, but CANNOT block or modify rights for Superadmin accounts.

TC-12: Standard User Access Restrictions
Given a standard User is logged in,
When attempting to access administrative endpoints or settings,

Then access is denied, and administrative controls (blocking users, changing rights) are hidden.
